invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: message_mod_prime returns without wiping low, which holds the
  message's low words times R reduced modulo the prime: a public number
  modulo a prime, which with that number gives the prime. Inside a
  signature a later call's frame is written over that one, so
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test calls the reduction on its own
  (test/rsa_sign_equiv_pieces.c), copies the stack below it and finds two
  words of the value there.

--- old
    rsa_mont64_add(o, low, high, mod);
    ct_wipe(low, sizeof low);
--- new
    rsa_mont64_add(o, low, high, mod);
